% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for toys, games, festive articles, sports equipment
% and fishing tackle, in the words of the tariff (Chapter 95). Each word
% cites the text that says what it means: the tariff's headings and notes,
% the EU explanatory notes to Chapter 95, US Customs rulings, and the
% description of the listings' fields (sources/listings/
% marketplace_fields_other_products.txt) for what a field means. Bridges.
%
% The fields read: the kind (Item Type, Type, Category, Product Type,
% Features, Use); the shop's category ("Toys & Hobbies > Stuffed Animals &
% Plush"); the occasion of a decoration (Occasion: Christmas); the words
% that name a pet toy (note 5).
%
% Left out, because no saved text says what the word means for the tariff:
%   - "model" alone: "Item Type: Model" is a scale model only in a toys
%     category of the shop (the rule below); elsewhere it can be a mannequin,
%     a display model or a part;
%   - "drone": a toy drone is of heading 9503 and an unmanned aircraft of
%     heading 8806 (CN EN to 9503: weight, height, range, no load); the word
%     does not decide;
%   - "scooter": a kick scooter is a toy (NY N272198), a scooter with a
%     motor is of heading 8711 above the CN EN limits;
%   - "game controller": a wired controller is of 9504.50, a wireless one of
%     8526 (NY N327482); the word does not say which;
%   - "Dolls & Accessories" as a shop category: it does not say whether the
%     product is a doll or an accessory (both are of heading 9503, but the
%     kind must be one of them);
%   - "blind box", "mystery box": no ruling names them; the toy inside
%     decides (NY N314012 classifies the surprise toy by itself);
%   - "Recommend Age": the age bands of heading 9503 are statistical lines
%     below six digits;
%   - "Sports & Entertainment > Cycling": most cycling goods are not of
%     Chapter 95 (bicycles, helmets, gloves, bells: note 1).
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* is in the shop category *a category*.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a field* is a field that names the kind.
    *a category* is a category of toys.
    *a name* is a word for the festivity *a festivity*.
    *a name* is a name of a decoration for *a festivity*.
    *a kind* is among the decoration kinds.
    *a name* is a pet toy word.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    *a good* is marketed as a decoration for *a festivity*.
    *a good* is identifiable as intended exclusively for animals.

